# PARTIAL FIX (qa-pr1179-r8, quality-mgr): AW.2 round-8 (fee01b959) added
# ac2_policy_selected_info_rows_reach_the_timeline,
# ac3_diagnostic_persistence_failure_does_not_poison_later_offers
# (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs), and
# ac4_prune_reduces_a_25k_fixture_to_the_documented_row_bound
# (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs), all independently
# confirmed genuine by quality-mgr, req-qa, and rust-qa-agent -- these close
# the AC2/AC3/AC4 portion of this finding. AC7's new test,
# ac7_saturation_state_transitions_from_degraded_to_recovered_after_quiet_window
# (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:496), only drives
# DegradationMonitor::observe() directly with a manually backdated
# degraded_since; it never exercises DiagnosticTimelineWriter::offer under a
# real paused-writer/queue-full scenario, and asserts no
# timeline_dropped_queue_full_total-equals-excess or single-emission
# guarantee. Confirmed independently by quality-mgr and req-qa (filed as
# req-qa's ATM-QA-AW2R8-001, Important); rust-qa-agent's pass did not flag
# this gap and does not overrule the two independent confirmations. This
# finding is narrowed to the remaining AC7 gap; status stays open/important.

